+### 자동 병합
+
+검사가 끝날 때까지 화면을 지켜보다가 직접 병합하는 대신, 열린 풀 리퀘스트에 자동 병합을 켤 수 있습니다. 그러면 현재 원본 커밋의 검사를 통과하는 시점에 OwnGit이 직접 병합합니다.
+
+```sh
+owngit pr auto-merge --number 1
+owngit pr auto-merge --number 1 --cancel
+```
+
+풀 리퀘스트 화면이나 소유자 API로도 켜거나 취소할 수 있습니다.
+
+```sh
+curl -X POST -u owngit:PASSWORD \
+  https://owngit.example.test/api/v1/repositories/example-project/pull-requests/1/auto-merge
+curl -X POST -u owngit:PASSWORD \
+  https://owngit.example.test/api/v1/repositories/example-project/pull-requests/1/auto-merge/cancel
+```
+
+알아 둘 점:
+
+- 이 의도는 커밋이 아니라 풀 리퀘스트에 속하므로 원본 브랜치에 푸시해도 유지됩니다. 병합 여부는 언제나 **현재** 원본과 대상 커밋을 기준으로 판단합니다.
+- OwnGit이 병합하는 것은 현재 원본 커밋의 최근 검사 증거가 최종 상태로 통과했고, 그 커밋을 깨끗한 작업 트리에서 실제로 테스트했으며, 해당 커밋에 커밋된 검사 구성을 사용했고, 읽을 수 있을 때뿐입니다. 증거가 없거나 검사가 진행 중이거나, 실패했거나, 작업 트리가 깨끗하지 않거나, 구성이 바뀌었거나, 기록을 읽을 수 없으면 풀 리퀘스트에 명확한 대기 또는 차단 상태가 표시되고 병합은 게시되지 않습니다.
+- 현재 커밋에 검사 증거가 전혀 없으면 검사가 구성되지 않은 경우에도 계속 기다립니다. 이후 체크 에이전트나 구성된 체크가 그 커밋의 통과 결과를 기록하면 병합합니다.
+- 원본 브랜치가 움직이면 예전 통과 결과는 재사용하지 않고 새 커밋의 검사를 기다립니다. 대상 브랜치가 움직이면 현재 커밋 쌍과 병합 가능성을 다시 확인하며, 충돌은 나중 ref 변경으로 해소될 때까지 대기 상태로만 둡니다.
+- 언제든 취소할 수 있습니다. 풀 리퀘스트를 닫아도 의도가 취소되며 다시 열 때 자동으로 되살아나지 않습니다. 취소나 닫기가 대기 중일 때 병합이 이미 게시되었다면 풀 리퀘스트는 병합됨으로 보고되고 두 번 병합되지 않습니다.
+- 대기 중인 의도는 서비스 재시작과 백업 복원 후에도 유지됩니다. 저장소를 일시적으로 사용할 수 없으면 의도를 유지하며 다음 검사 완료나 ref 변경 때 다시 시도합니다.
+- 자동 병합을 켜지 않으면 달라지는 것은 없습니다. 검사와 리뷰는 계속 참고용이고, 검사가 실패하거나 실행 중이어도 수동 `pr merge`는 이전과 똑같이 동작합니다.
+
 ## 체크 기록하기
 
 `owngit check` 명령(체크 에이전트)은 내 컴퓨터에서 프로젝트 체크를 실행하고 테스트한 바로 그 커밋에 묶어 결과를 서버에 기록합니다. [체크 에이전트 토큰](#체크-에이전트-토큰)이 필요합니다. 푸시할 때마다 OwnGit이 직접 실행하는 체크는 [자동 체크](AUTOMATIC_CHECKS.ko.md)를 보세요.
diff --git a/docs/CODING_TOOLS.md b/docs/CODING_TOOLS.md
index 89152f4..5a964bd 100644
--- a/docs/CODING_TOOLS.md
+++ b/docs/CODING_TOOLS.md
@@ -251,6 +251,56 @@ What to know:
 - `pr list` shows 50 pull requests at a time, newest first. When more remain,
   the result has `next`; pass it as `--before` for the next page.
 
+### Automatic merge
+
+Instead of watching the page and merging by hand after checks finish, enable
+automatic merging on an open pull request. OwnGit then merges it itself once
+the current source commit's checks pass.
+
+```sh
+owngit pr auto-merge --number 1
+owngit pr auto-merge --number 1 --cancel
+```
+
+You can also enable or cancel it from the pull request page, or with the owner
+API:
+
+```sh
+curl -X POST -u owngit:PASSWORD \
+  https://owngit.example.test/api/v1/repositories/example-project/pull-requests/1/auto-merge
+curl -X POST -u owngit:PASSWORD \
+  https://owngit.example.test/api/v1/repositories/example-project/pull-requests/1/auto-merge/cancel
+```
+
+What to know:
+
+- The intent belongs to the pull request, not to a commit: it survives a push
+  to the source branch. The merge is always decided for the **current** source
+  and target commits.
+- OwnGit merges only when the latest check evidence of the current source
+  commit finished with a pass, really tested that commit from a clean worktree,
+  used the check configuration committed at that commit, and was readable.
+  Missing evidence, checks still running, a failed verdict, a dirty worktree, a
+  changed configuration, or an unreadable record shows a clear waiting or
+  blocked state on the pull request and publishes no merge.
+- With no check evidence at all for the current commit, the request keeps
+  waiting, even when no checks are configured. It merges once a helper or
+  configured check records a passing result for that commit.
+- When the source branch moves, an older pass is never reused; the request
+  waits for checks of the new commit. When the target branch moves, OwnGit
+  re-checks the current pair and its mergeability, and a conflict only waits
+  until a later ref change resolves it.
+- You can cancel at any time. Closing a pull request cancels the intent too;
+  reopening does not bring it back. If a merge was already published while a
+  cancel or close was queued, the pull request is reported as merged and is not
+  merged twice.
+- Pending intents survive a restart and backup restore. When the repository is
+  temporarily unavailable, OwnGit keeps the intent and retries on the next
+  check completion or ref change.
+- Without automatic merging, nothing changes: checks and reviews stay
+  advisory and manual `pr merge` works exactly as before, including while
+  checks fail or are still running.
+
 ## Recording checks
 
 `owngit check` (the helper) runs a project's checks on your own computer
diff --git a/internal/automerge/coordinator.go b/internal/automerge/coordinator.go
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..83021be
--- /dev/null
+++ b/internal/automerge/coordinator.go
@@ -0,0 +1,169 @@
+// Package automerge runs the background convergence of pull requests whose
+// owners enabled automatic merging. A wake asks the coordinator to process
+// one bounded page of each repository with an enabled intent; the pull
+// request service decides, under its repository lock, whether a request is
+// still waiting, blocked, or merges now. Repeated wakes coalesce, and a
+// minute-granularity ticker retries requests that wait on a conflict or a
+// temporarily unavailable repository.
+package automerge
+
+import (
+	"context"
+	"sync"
+	"time"
+
+	"owngit/internal/pullrequest"
+)
+
+// pageSize bounds how many intents one scan page processes per repository.
+// One page covers every normal installation; the cursor rotates fairly past
+// larger sets across wakes.
+const pageSize = 64
+
+// defaultInterval is the safety-net retry cadence. Event wakes drive the
+// normal convergence.
+const defaultInterval = 5 * time.Minute
+
+// Store is the state read the coordinator needs. *state.Store satisfies it.
+type Store interface {
+	RepositoriesWithPullRequestAutoMerges(ctx context.Context) ([]string, error)
+}
+
+// PullRequests is the converging part of the pull request service.
+// *pullrequest.Service satisfies it.
+type PullRequests interface {
+	ConvergeAutoMerge(ctx context.Context, repositoryID string, number int64) (bool, *pullrequest.View, error)
+	ConvergeAutoMerges(ctx context.Context, repositoryID string, after int64, limit int) (int64, bool, error)
+}
+
+// Coordinator coalesces wake signals into bounded convergence scans. Its zero
+// value is not ready; construct one with New.
+type Coordinator struct {
+	Store        Store
+	PullRequests PullRequests
+	Logf         func(string, ...any)
+	Interval     time.Duration
+
+	startOnce sync.Once
+	stopOnce  sync.Once
+	wake      chan struct{}
+	ctx       context.Context
+	cancel    context.CancelFunc
+	done      chan struct{}
+
+	cursorsMu sync.Mutex
+	cursors   map[string]int64
+}
+
+// New builds a coordinator.
+func New(store Store, service PullRequests, logf func(string, ...any)) *Coordinator {
+	if logf == nil {
+		logf = func(string, ...any) {}
+	}
+	return &Coordinator{
+		Store: store, PullRequests: service, Logf: logf,
+		Interval: defaultInterval, cursors: make(map[string]int64),
+	}
+}
+
+// Start launches the loop and queues one immediate scan, which converges
+// intents that survived a restart or a restore.
+func (c *Coordinator) Start(ctx context.Context) {
+	c.startOnce.Do(func() {
+		c.ctx, c.cancel = context.WithCancel(ctx)
+		c.wake = make(chan struct{}, 1)
+		c.done = make(chan struct{})
+		c.wake <- struct{}{}
+		go c.loop()
+	})
+}
+
+// Stop ends the loop and waits for the running scan to finish.
+func (c *Coordinator) Stop() {
+	c.stopOnce.Do(func() {
+		if c.cancel != nil {
+			c.cancel()
+			<-c.done
+		}
+	})
+}
+
+// Wake queues a convergence scan. Signals while one is queued or running
+// coalesce, and a wake before Start or after Stop is a no-op.
+func (c *Coordinator) Wake(string) {
+	if c.wake == nil {
+		return
+	}
+	select {
+	case c.wake <- struct{}{}:
+	default:
+	}
+}
+
+func (c *Coordinator) loop() {
+	defer close(c.done)
+	interval := c.Interval
+	if interval <= 0 {
+		interval = defaultInterval
+	}
+	ticker := time.NewTicker(interval)
+	defer ticker.Stop()
+	for {
+		select {
+		case <-c.ctx.Done():
+			return
+		case <-c.wake:
+			c.scan(c.ctx)
+		case <-ticker.C:
+			c.scan(c.ctx)
+		}
+	}
+}
+
+// scan processes one bounded page of every repository with an enabled intent.
+// It is also called directly by tests.
+func (c *Coordinator) scan(ctx context.Context) {
+	repositories, err := c.Store.RepositoriesWithPullRequestAutoMerges(ctx)
+	if err != nil {
+		c.Logf("auto-merge scan could not list repositories: %v", err)
+		return
+	}
+	for _, repositoryID := range repositories {
+		if ctx.Err() != nil {
+			return
+		}
+		after := c.cursor(repositoryID)
+		next, more, err := c.PullRequests.ConvergeAutoMerges(ctx, repositoryID, after, pageSize)
+		if err != nil {
+			c.Logf("auto-merge convergence in repository %s will retry: %v", repositoryID, err)
+		}
+		if !more {
+			c.resetCursor(repositoryID)
+			continue
+		}
+		c.setCursor(repositoryID, next)
+	}
+}
+
+// Scan exposes one convergence round to callers outside the loop.
+func (c *Coordinator) Scan(ctx context.Context) {
+	c.scan(ctx)
+}
+
+func (c *Coordinator) cursor(repositoryID string) int64 {
+	c.cursorsMu.Lock()
+	defer c.cursorsMu.Unlock()
+	return c.cursors[repositoryID]
+}
+
+func (c *Coordinator) setCursor(repositoryID string, after int64) {
+	c.cursorsMu.Lock()
+	defer c.cursorsMu.Unlock()
+	c.cursors[repositoryID] = after
+}
+
+func (c *Coordinator) resetCursor(repositoryID string) {
+	c.cursorsMu.Lock()
+	defer c.cursorsMu.Unlock()
+	delete(c.cursors, repositoryID)
+}
diff --git a/internal/automerge/coordinator_test.go b/internal/automerge/coordinator_test.go
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5368d7d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/internal/automerge/coordinator_test.go
@@ -0,0 +1,230 @@
+package automerge
+
+import (
+	"context"
+	"errors"
+	"sync"
+	"testing"
+	"time"
+
+	"owngit/internal/pullrequest"
+)
+
+type fakeStore struct {
+	repositories []string
+	err          error
+}
+
+func (s *fakeStore) RepositoriesWithPullRequestAutoMerges(context.Context) ([]string, error) {
+	return s.repositories, s.err
+}
+
+type fakePullRequests struct {
+	mu          sync.Mutex
+	pages       map[string][]int64
+	converged   []string
+	convergeErr error
+	started     chan struct{}
+	finished    chan struct{}
+	block       chan struct{}
+}
+
+func (f *fakePullRequests) ConvergeAutoMerge(context.Context, string, int64) (bool, *pullrequest.View, error) {
+	return false, nil, nil
+}
+
+func (f *fakePullRequests) ConvergeAutoMerges(ctx context.Context, repositoryID string, after int64, limit int) (int64, bool, error) {
+	if f.started != nil {
+		select {
+		case f.started <- struct{}{}:
+		default:
+		}
+	}
+	// A blocking page models an operation that cannot interrupt itself: Stop
+	// must wait for it to return rather than closing the loop under it.
+	if f.block != nil {
+		<-f.block
+	}
+	f.mu.Lock()
+	f.converged = append(f.converged, repositoryID)
+	page := f.pages[repositoryID]
+	f.mu.Unlock()
+	// Circular page semantics matching the store: hand back the page after
+	// after, with more while rows remain.
+	var ordered []int64
+	for _, number := range page {
+		if number > after {
+			ordered = append(ordered, number)
+		}
+	}
+	for _, number := range page {
+		if number <= after {
+			ordered = append(ordered, number)
+		}
+	}
+	if limit < len(ordered) {
+		ordered = ordered[:limit]
+	}
+	if f.finished != nil {
+		select {
+		case f.finished <- struct{}{}:
+		default:
+		}
+	}
+	if len(ordered) == 0 {
+		return 0, false, f.convergeErr
+	}
+	more := len(page) > len(ordered) || after != 0
+	return ordered[len(ordered)-1], more, f.convergeErr
+}
+
+func newCoordinator(t *testing.T, store Store, service PullRequests) *Coordinator {
+	t.Helper()
+	return New(store, service, func(string, ...any) {})
+}
+
+func TestWakeCoalescesIntoOneScan(t *testing.T) {
+	ctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(context.Background())
+	defer cancel()
+	runs := make(chan struct{}, 16)
+	store := &fakeStore{repositories: []string{"alpha"}}
+	service := &countingPullRequests{runs: runs}
+	coordinator := newCoordinator(t, store, service)
+	coordinator.Interval = time.Hour
+	coordinator.Start(ctx)
+	for i := 0; i < 10; i++ {
+		coordinator.Wake("alpha")
+	}
+	// The first scan already ran at Start; wait for at least one queued scan
+	// to drain, then give the coalesced loop a moment to prove no more follow.
+	<-runs
+	coordinator.Wake("alpha")
+	<-runs
+	select {
+	case <-runs:
+		t.Fatal("coalesced wakes produced another scan")
+	case <-time.After(20 * time.Millisecond):
+	}
+	if got := service.count(); got > 3 {
+		t.Fatalf("11 wakes produced %d scans", got)
+	}
+	coordinator.Stop()
+}
+
+type countingPullRequests struct {
+	mu   sync.Mutex
+	n    int
+	runs chan struct{}
+}
+
+func (c *countingPullRequests) ConvergeAutoMerge(context.Context, string, int64) (bool, *pullrequest.View, error) {
+	return false, nil, nil
+}
+
+func (c *countingPullRequests) ConvergeAutoMerges(context.Context, string, int64, int) (int64, bool, error) {
+	c.mu.Lock()
+	c.n++
+	c.mu.Unlock()
+	select {
+	case c.runs <- struct{}{}:
+	default:
+	}
+	return 0, false, nil
+}
+
+func (c *countingPullRequests) count() int {
+	c.mu.Lock()
+	defer c.mu.Unlock()
+	return c.n
+}
+
+func TestScanTouchesOnlyRepositoriesWithIntents(t *testing.T) {
+	store := &fakeStore{repositories: nil}
+	service := &countingPullRequests{runs: make(chan struct{}, 4)}
+	coordinator := newCoordinator(t, store, service)
+	coordinator.Scan(context.Background())
+	if got := service.count(); got != 0 {
+		t.Fatalf("scan without intents converged %d repositories", got)
+	}
+
+	store.repositories = []string{"alpha", "beta"}
+	service2 := &fakePullRequests{pages: map[string][]int64{
+		"alpha": {1, 3, 5},
+		"beta":  {7},
+	}}
+	coordinator2 := newCoordinator(t, store, service2)
+	coordinator2.Scan(context.Background())
+	service2.mu.Lock()
+	got := append([]string(nil), service2.converged...)
+	service2.mu.Unlock()
+	if len(got) != 2 || got[0] != "alpha" || got[1] != "beta" {
+		t.Fatalf("scan converged %v", got)
+	}
+}
+
+func TestScanPagesFairlyAcrossRounds(t *testing.T) {
+	store := &fakeStore{repositories: []string{"alpha"}}
+	service := &fakePullRequests{pages: map[string][]int64{"alpha": {1, 3, 5, 7, 9}}}
+	coordinator := newCoordinator(t, store, service)
+	// One page of 2 per scan. The cursor rotates and eventually visits every
+	// intent instead of starving the higher numbers.
+	seen := make(map[int64]bool)
+	for i := 0; i < 4; i++ {
+		coordinator.Scan(context.Background())
+	}
+	// Re-read the cursor path by converging directly: assert all numbers were
+	// offered through successive pages using the store's paging shape.
+	after := int64(0)
+	for page := 0; page < 4; page++ {
+		next, _, err := service.ConvergeAutoMerges(context.Background(), "alpha", after, 2)
+		if err != nil {
+			t.Fatal(err)
+		}
+		seen[next] = true
+		after = next
+	}
+	if len(seen) < 4 {
+		t.Fatalf("fair paging offered %d pages: %v", len(seen), seen)
+	}
+}
+
+func TestScanContinuesWhenOneConvergenceFails(t *testing.T) {
+	store := &fakeStore{repositories: []string{"alpha", "beta"}}
+	service := &fakePullRequests{
+		pages:       map[string][]int64{"alpha": {1}, "beta": {2}},
+		convergeErr: errors.New("repository busy"),
+	}
+	coordinator := newCoordinator(t, store, service)
+	coordinator.Scan(context.Background() /* the error is logged, not raised */)
+	service.mu.Lock()
+	got := append([]string(nil), service.converged...)
+	service.mu.Unlock()
+	if len(got) != 2 {
+		t.Fatalf("one repository failure stopped the scan: %v", got)
+	}
+}
+
+func TestStopWaitsForRunningScan(t *testing.T) {
+	ctx := context.Background()
+	block := make(chan struct{})
+	started := make(chan struct{}, 1)
+	store := &fakeStore{repositories: []string{"alpha"}}
+	service := &fakePullRequests{pages: map[string][]int64{"alpha": {1}}, block: block, started: started}
+	coordinator := newCoordinator(t, store, service)
+	coordinator.Start(ctx)
+	<-started
+	stopped := make(chan struct{})
+	go func() {
+		coordinator.Stop()
+		close(stopped)
+	}()
+	select {
+	case <-stopped:
+		t.Fatal("Stop returned while the scan was blocked")
+	case <-time.After(20 * time.Millisecond):
+	}
+	close(block)
+	<-stopped
+	// Wakes after stop do nothing.
+	coordinator.Wake("alpha")
+}
diff --git a/internal/automerge/integration_test.go b/internal/automerge/integration_test.go
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..881d067
